  "summary": "Reference for the words that ship with images, charts, and infographics: alt text, captions, chart titles, axis labels, and annotations. The image is half the message. This skill is the other half.",
  "facets": [
    {
      "title": "Visual Writing",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Reference for the words that ship with images, charts, and infographics: alt text, captions, chart titles, axis labels, and annotations. The image is half the message. This skill is the other half.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/visual-writing/#visual-writing",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "The one rule: visual writing makes images legible without the image",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Every other rule in this skill follows from one premise: a reader who cannot see the image must still receive the load-bearing information. That reader may be a blind user with a screen reader, a sighted user on a slow network, a sighted user skimming for the chart's takeaway, or a search engine indexing the page.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/visual-writing/#the-one-rule-visual-writing-makes-images-legible-without-the-image",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "The alt text serves the screen reader.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/visual-writing/#the-one-rule-visual-writing-makes-images-legible-without-the-image",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "The caption serves the skimmer.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/visual-writing/#the-one-rule-visual-writing-makes-images-legible-without-the-image",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "The chart title serves the takeaway.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/visual-writing/#the-one-rule-visual-writing-makes-images-legible-without-the-image",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "The annotation serves the trend.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/visual-writing/#the-one-rule-visual-writing-makes-images-legible-without-the-image",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "They are four jobs, not one.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/visual-writing/#the-one-rule-visual-writing-makes-images-legible-without-the-image",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Core concept 1 — The alt-text triple",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Alt text answers three questions:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/visual-writing/#core-concept-1-the-alt-text-triple",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "What's there? - concrete, observable content",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/visual-writing/#core-concept-1-the-alt-text-triple",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Why is it there? - the function the image serves in the page",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/visual-writing/#core-concept-1-the-alt-text-triple",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "What does it show? - the specific information a sighted reader gets",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/visual-writing/#core-concept-1-the-alt-text-triple",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Core concept 3 — Caption vs alt text vs long description",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Alt text is for users who cannot see the image. It lives in alt=\"\". Typically 5 to 15 words.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/visual-writing/#core-concept-3-caption-vs-alt-text-vs-long-description",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Caption is visible to everyone. It lives in <figcaption>. Adds context, attribution.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/visual-writing/#core-concept-3-caption-vs-alt-text-vs-long-description",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Long description is a structured prose alternative for complex images.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/visual-writing/#core-concept-3-caption-vs-alt-text-vs-long-description",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Anti-pattern: duplication. If alt=\"Sales rose 18% in Q4\" and the caption reads the same, the screen-reader user hears it twice.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/visual-writing/#core-concept-3-caption-vs-alt-text-vs-long-description",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Core concept 4 — Tufte's principles",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Above all else, show the data. Title and labels exist to disclose the data.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/visual-writing/#core-concept-4-tuftes-principles",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Maximize the data-ink ratio. Erase ink that doesn't carry data.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/visual-writing/#core-concept-4-tuftes-principles",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Erase redundant data-ink. A bar chart with a legend, title, axis labels, and a redundant data table embeds the same fact four times.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/visual-writing/#core-concept-4-tuftes-principles",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Reject chartjunk. Heavy gridlines, moiré fills, 3-D effects, drop shadows.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/visual-writing/#core-concept-4-tuftes-principles",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Use sparklines for in-line trend. Caption a sparkline like a word - usually with just the latest value.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/visual-writing/#core-concept-4-tuftes-principles",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Core concept 5 — The Knaflic \"action title\" rule",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "The chart title states the takeaway. The axis labels confirm it.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/visual-writing/#core-concept-5-the-knaflic-action-title-rule",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Generic title (descriptive only):",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/visual-writing/#core-concept-5-the-knaflic-action-title-rule",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "> Quarterly Revenue, 2023–2024",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/visual-writing/#core-concept-5-the-knaflic-action-title-rule",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Action title (takeaway-bearing):",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/visual-writing/#core-concept-5-the-knaflic-action-title-rule",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "> Q4 2024 revenue exceeded plan by 18% - the strongest quarter on record",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/visual-writing/#core-concept-5-the-knaflic-action-title-rule",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Rule of thumb: no chart without a takeaway. If you cannot state in one sentence what the chart is for, either find the takeaway or delete the chart.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/visual-writing/#core-concept-5-the-knaflic-action-title-rule",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Core concept 6 — Axis labels",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Label the units. \"Revenue (USD millions)\" not \"Revenue.\"",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/visual-writing/#core-concept-6-axis-labels",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Date axes get human dates. \"Jan 2024\" - not raw timestamps, not \"Q1\".",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/visual-writing/#core-concept-6-axis-labels",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Avoid axis label rotation. If labels overflow horizontally, the chart probably has too many categories.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/visual-writing/#core-concept-6-axis-labels",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Core concept 7 — Annotations",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "An annotation is a written assertion attached to a specific data point. Use annotations for:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/visual-writing/#core-concept-7-annotations",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "The single highest or lowest point (\"peak: 8,420 - Aug 14\")",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/visual-writing/#core-concept-7-annotations",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "A regime change (\"← deploy of v2.3\")",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/visual-writing/#core-concept-7-annotations",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "An anomaly (\"backfill artifact; ignore\")",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/visual-writing/#core-concept-7-annotations",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Annotations are journalism inside a chart. Empty annotations (\"note this\") are wasted ink.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/visual-writing/#core-concept-7-annotations",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Core concept 8 — Accessible data-viz captioning",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "The \"describe the trend, then the value\" pattern:",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/visual-writing/#core-concept-8-accessible-data-viz-captioning",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "> Sales increased steadily from January to July, then declined through December. The peak was 8,420 units in July. The lowest month was December at 3,100 units.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/visual-writing/#core-concept-8-accessible-data-viz-captioning",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "Anti-pattern: read every value.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/visual-writing/#core-concept-8-accessible-data-viz-captioning",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "> January was 4,200, February was 4,800, March was 5,100...",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/visual-writing/#core-concept-8-accessible-data-viz-captioning",
          "note": null
        },
        {
          "text": "If every value matters, provide a <table> and skip the chart alt-text recital.",
          "source": "https://llms-explorer.com/sources/mdb-context-hub/visual-writing/#core-concept-8-accessible-data-viz-captioning",
          "note": null
        }
      ]
    },
